A||||12||Alex2004||How much would it cost to have new power locks installed?||||1||
Z||000000||Alex2004||01-15-2001||07:42 PM||||my car has factory power locks, and the drivers door takes about 3 pushes to lock it, but unlock is just one, the passenger works fine, i took the door panel off and was messing with the (hitter thing that hits the bar) and that didn't fix it.  I did that before to get the unlock to work rite.  I am planning on getting an alarm/keyless entry soon so i am just wondering how much would it cost to have completely new power lock motors installed.  Anyone have an idea?  Thanks...<P>Alex||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-15-2001||07:59 PM||||Try posting a thread at the mall, you'll probably only have to replace the lock motors.  Someone's probably got a good working set, like fierodave.  If you've already got the panel off, you should be able to replace them yourself.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||01-15-2001||08:15 PM||||could also be a relay getting cruddy. You might want to replace those first since they are probably easier to get to.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||01-15-2001||08:15 PM||||yep, with your panel off its ez. just take out mounting bolt and unplug connector. Its just a solenoid. Im guessing all GM ones are pretty much same. Autozone or parts place might even have them on rack. Usually the prob is just lots of dried up caked up grease and grime. Lots of spray cleaner, then some silicone spray may fix it. You can get a complete kit with your alarm to replace everything.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex2004||01-15-2001||08:26 PM||||i meant the interior door panel.  Where are the relay's at for the door locks?  But if it's only the driver's side lock that is bad do you still think it is a relay? let me know, thanks.  Oh and how much do you think it will cost? Thanks, <BR>Alex...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mark||01-15-2001||09:41 PM||||Alex,<P>Mine did the same thing. As Roger suggested, I lubricated everything that moves with something like WD40.  Works fine now.||||reg||1
Z||000006||286SE'S||01-17-2001||02:10 PM||||The power lock relay is way up above the passenger's footwell on the outside wall.<BR>It is hard to see with the dashboard in. It is two silver relays mounted on a plate. I don't believe that is the cause of one lock not working. The same power is sent to both locks at the same time. They are NOT solenoids. They are motors. Same on both sides. I have tested these on a bench and they have a very strong push/pull. In the car they do not seem to get as much current and are weaker. Must be due to long wire lengths.<BR>A new one should be a common GM part. They were used in so many cars.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Carrolles||01-17-2001||02:18 PM||||Try dribbling a little WD-40 down the shaft of the actuator.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex2004||01-17-2001||05:47 PM||||Ok, thanks... i am going to put WD 40 on in a while, i should have though of that before! LOL... Thanks!<P>Alex...||||reg||10
Z||000009||Lisa 86 2m4||01-17-2001||07:41 PM||||Alex,<BR>That sounds like what my car was doing-exactly! Besides lubing everything that moved in the door, I also replaced the lock cyclinders-unbelievable how rusted they were! There is a pin/plate that the door-slide hooks into that pivots the cylinder, that was so rusted I spent quite awhile sanding the rust off of those, thickly coating them with silicon grease before reattcahing to the new cylinders. If this pin is rusted, that alone could result in the locks not locking- too much resistance for the cylinder to pivot.  I also did all of this because I was installing keyless entry. It was the most frustrating thing I have ever done, but I love my keyless entry!!!<p>[This message has been edited by Lisa 86 2m4 (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Alex2004||01-17-2001||08:39 PM||||well i went outside and took the inside panel off, and i wd40'd some of it, i wasn't sure what exactly to do, but i sprayed it on the little circle thing that kinda looks like a spring, and in the thing that goes up and down, it has a plastic deal over it! LOL, umm, it didn't really do anything. So can sometime tell me exactly what to do to make it work better?  Cause i am confused with it.  Oh, sometimes when i am messing with the locks trying to see if it worked, it will sometimes lock half way, and then i can hear the relay clicking but the locks don't do anything, so i manualy lock it and then click unlock and it works fine, do you know why that happens?  Oh, when i push the lock button it will move alittle and then again if i hold it down it will move slowly. But if you can tell me exactly what to do to fix it, it would help alot! Thanks<P>Alex...||||reg||4
Z||000011||mbramble||01-18-2001||12:17 PM||||I'm not sure anyone will be able to tell you exactly what to do without actually looking at your door to see what the problem is.  <P>Here is the problem I had with the power doors I put on my car.  My problem was on the passenger side and just the opposite of yours; it wouldn't unlock, but locked with no problem.  What I found was that the pushrod (that goes from the 'manaul' lock knob in the inner door latch all the way to the back of the door) was bent right at the 'slide' that it snaps into.  It could freely move one direction, but in the other direction the bend caused it to bind in the 'slide'.  I straightened the rod and it works fine.<P>You just have to look and look as you lock/unlock to see what your particular trouble is.<P>Good luck!!||||reg||1
Z||000012||GarethWright||01-19-2001||05:26 PM||||Erm I'm not sure if this will work with the locks, but when my power mirrors wouldn't work properly (would run, but only after several presses of the rocker button) I cleaned out the contacts Inside the switch with a paper towel and that fixed it right away. Apparently the old grease was so clogged with crud it wasnt letting the contacts, erm well.. Contact.  Good luck with it.<BR>Gareth||||reg||1
